  "answer": "## What needs to be added for “Badge” (material-next)\n\nFrom the PR description, the intent is to **copy the existing `Badge` component from `material`**, then **migrate it to TypeScript** and update it to match the v5 “Material You / CSS variables” conventions.\n\n### CSS Variables convention\nThe PR explicitly sets the naming convention:\n- Component variables use `--md-comp` + component name\n- For Badge: `--md-comp-badge`\n\nThis is described directly in the issue text (no source excerpt shown here), but it matches the wider direction evidenced by the repo’s CSS-vars provider architecture (e.g., `packages/mui-material/src/styles/CssVarsProvider.tsx` is already present per the style entrypoint deps listing in `packages/mui-material/src/styles/index.js`).\n\n### ThemeProvider removal / move to CssVarsProvider\nThe change list says to **drop `ThemeProvider` in favor of `CssVarsProvider`**. The repo still contains `ThemeProvider` (see `packages/mui-material/src/styles/ThemeProvider.js`), but the direction is to rely on `CssVarsProvider` instead for new/updated components. (See that `packages/mui-material/src/styles/index.js` depends on `packages/mui-material/src/styles/CssVarsProvider.tsx`.)\n\n### Where Badge is expected to plug in\nAlthough the retrieved wiki excerpts don’t include the Badge source itself, the docs/build already reference `Badge`:\n- `docs/data/material/getting-started/templates/dashboard/Dashboard.js` imports `packages/mui-material/src/Badge/index.js` (listed in its dependency graph).\n\n## Architecture implication (implementation steps)\n1. Create `packages/mui-material/src/Badge/index.tsx` (and related TS files as needed) based on material’s Badge.\n2. Implement styles driven by CSS vars using the `--md-comp-badge` token prefix.\n3. Ensure styling uses the v5/CSS-vars system (via `CssVarsProvider`), not the legacy `ThemeProvider`.\n\nIf you share the retrieved excerpt for the actual `Badge` symbol/source (e.g., `packages/mui-material/src/Badge/...`), I can map these requirements to the exact exported types, slots, and styling hooks used in this repo.",
